meta {
  name: Update Workflow Metadata via public-api (unverified)
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/workflow/{{testWorkflowId}}
  body: json
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  apiKey: {{apiKey}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "title": "Automatic Assignment Workflow"
  }
}

docs {
  UNVERIFIED. The GET on this same api.jotform.com path works with just
  an apiKey (surprised us, see get-workflow-undocumented.bru) unlike its
  www.jotform.com/API counterpart which is CSRF-blocked. Does POST here
  also work? Sends the same title back (non-destructive) so a 200
  doesn't silently change anything before we've decided this is safe to
  build a real tool on.
}
